{"name":"Pelican Bay","hex":"#9eacb1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pelican","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various seabirds of the family Pelecanidae, having a long bill with a distendable pouch.","A native or resident of the American state of Louisiana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pelican"},{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pelican Bay, Florida","blocks":[{"text":"Pelican Bay is a census-designated place (CDP) in Collier County, Florida, United States. The population was 6,660 at the 2020 census, up from 6,346 at the 2010 census. It is part of the Naples–Marco Island Metropolitan Statistical Area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Collier_County_Florida_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Pelican_Bay_Highlighted.svg/330px-Collier_County_Florida_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Pelican_Bay_Highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelican_Bay%2C_Florida","wikidata":"Q2393650"},{"title":"Pelican Bay, Texas","blocks":[{"text":"Pelican Bay is a city in the far northwest corner of Tarrant County, Texas, on the shore of Eagle Mountain Lake. Founded by Olen Yandell on his struggling dairy farm in 1970, it incorporated in 1981. Despite Yandell's aspirations to create a new Sausalito, Calif., Pelican Bay remains a modest enclave. The large majority of residences are mobile homes. The population was 2,049 at the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Tarrant_County_Texas_Incorporated_Areas_Pelican_Bay_highlighted.svg/330px-Tarrant_County_Texas_Incorporated_Areas_Pelican_Bay_highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelican_Bay%2C_Texas","wikidata":"Q977943"},{"title":"Pelican","blocks":[{"text":"Pelicans are a genus of large water birds that make up the family Pelecanidae. They are characterized by a long beak and a large throat pouch used for catching prey and draining water from the scooped-up contents before swallowing. They have predominantly pale plumage, except for the brown and Peruvian pelicans. The bills, pouches, and bare facial skin of all pelicans become brightly coloured before the breeding season."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Pelikan_Walvis_Bay.jpg/330px-Pelikan_Walvis_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelican","wikidata":"Q19413"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg/500px-Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thum